(:id "go/F12" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/gotable/fixedroadmap_t13_test.go: TestFixedRoadmapGoT13SecondLayoutUnderHeldHash") :tested-revision "5b0c960613553fca4d19745792174ef7c956327c" :note "docs/FIXED-FORM-ALGORITHM.md §5.3 step 5: \"a known hash over different bytes is layout_malformed\" — a second layout for a hash the reader holds is refused by that one name, at the header read, before any record is parsed and with the destination and the report counters untouched. The card closes go/F12 with the refusal that already exists (Glenn, 2026-10-13: \"ok then do layout_malformed\"); no new error name is added in code, spec or roadmap. The go port of c's cT01SecondLayout bends one held layout byte and shifts a length-off-by-one copy, both under the same header hash.")
